# What `docker build` must NOT copy into the build context.
#
# There is no Dockerfile yet — this file exists first on purpose. The default
# without it is to copy the entire working tree, and the two entries that matter
# most (.env and node_modules) are mistakes you only notice much later: a secret
# baked into an image layer survives being deleted in a later layer, and a
# host-built native module fails at runtime on a different platform.

# Secrets. `.env` in an image layer is readable by anyone who can pull it, and
# `docker history` will still show it after a later RUN deletes the file.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.cer
*.crt

# Dependencies must be installed INSIDE the image, never copied in. argon2 is a
# native module: a macOS-built binary copied into a Linux image does not merely
# bloat it, it crashes on first hash.
node_modules
**/node_modules
.pnpm-store

# Build output — the image builds its own, and stale local output silently
# shadowing a fresh build is a genuinely confusing failure.
dist
**/dist
build
**/build
.turbo
**/.turbo
*.tsbuildinfo

# History and tooling: large, and never needed at runtime.
.git
.github
.vscode
.idea
.claude

# Local-only
docker-compose.yml
docker-data
coverage
test-results
playwright-report
*.log
.DS_Store

# Docs and design assets are not part of any runtime image.
docs
README.md
CLAUDE.md
